##### Use Gum for Banners 
---------------------------------------------

Even though {{site.api_link('io.print.banner',mkdocs,arg='label')}} detects terminal width, it isn't fancy otherwise.  A related target is {{site.api_link('io.draw.banner',mkdocs,arg='label')}}, which prints dividers with [charmbracelet/gum](https://github.com/charmbracelet/gum).

{{macros.img_link("demo-gum.gif", mkdocs, "90%")}}


##### Banners with Figlet
-----------------------------

You can also use a (dockerized) version of the `figlet` tool, like this:

```bash {.cli_example .language-bash}

# or, ./compose.mk io.figlet/banner
$ label=banner ./compose.mk io.figlet
```
```markdown {.cli_output}
 ██                                                
░██                                                
░██       ██████   ███████  ███████   █████  ██████
░██████  ░░░░░░██ ░░██░░░██░░██░░░██ ██░░░██░░██░░█
░██░░░██  ███████  ░██  ░██ ░██  ░██░███████ ░██ ░ 
░██  ░██ ██░░░░██  ░██  ░██ ░██  ░██░██░░░░  ░██   
░██████ ░░████████ ███  ░██ ███  ░██░░██████░███   
 ░░░░░    ░░░░░░░░ ░░░   ░░ ░░░   ░░  ░░░░░░ ░░░    
```

To add color, you can use a context manager and any of the colors that `compose.mk` natively understands.

```bash {.cli_example} 
./compose.mk io.with.color/red,io.figlet/banner
```

For other TUI-components like this that fall short of a full-blown interface,  see [these docs for stand-alone mode]({{_}}/tool-overview). See also the [full documentation for all `io.*` targets]({{_}}/api/#api-io)

